    {'subject':'Chemistry','topic':'Reactions','topic_code':'C4','difficulty':1,
     'question_text':'What colour is copper sulfate solution?',
     'option_a':'Colourless','option_b':'Orange-brown','option_c':'Blue','option_d':'Pale green',
     'correct_answer':'C','explanation':'Cu²⁺ ions give copper sulfate solution a characteristic blue colour.','correction_tip':'Cu²⁺ = blue. Fe²⁺ = pale green. Fe³⁺ = orange-brown. Remember these ion colours.'},

    {'subject':'Chemistry','topic':'Reactions','topic_code':'C4','difficulty':1,
     'question_text':'Which acid produces nitrate salts?',
     'option_a':'Hydrochloric acid','option_b':'Sulfuric acid','option_c':'Nitric acid','option_d':'Phosphoric acid',
     'correct_answer':'C','explanation':'HNO₃ (nitric acid) produces nitrate salts when it reacts with metals, metal oxides, carbonates, or alkalis.','correction_tip':'HCl→chloride, H₂SO₄→sulfate, HNO₃→nitrate, H₃PO₄→phosphate.'},

